    {
      "etag": "\"7cb802049d46d0713bdebe4c563ffd5f\"",
      "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/annotations/bbf45842-36e4-44c2-b398-e6169146c6c6/",
      "type": "Annotation",
      "created": "2026-11-14T14:33:18.131885+00:00",
      "modified": "2026-11-14T14:33:18.131895+00:00",
      "dc:source": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/sources/1228/",
      "target": {
        "source": {
          "id": "http://cudl.lib.cam.ac.uk/iiif/MS-TS-NS-00297-00242/canvas/1",
          "type": "Canvas",
          "partOf": {
            "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/documents/24828/iiif/manifest/"
          }
        },
        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:171.561767578125,209.5028533935547,2975.10205078125,4429.591384887695",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\nThe letter of [my lord, the shaykh \u2026 may God prolong his life,] arrived,\n</li>\n<li>\nand may He perpetuate his glory and blessings, and never deprive him of His gracious [guidance \u2026 and may He be for him]\n</li>\n<li>\na protector and guardian in all his affairs. I congratulate [him] on these\n</li>\n<li>\nblessed festivals. May God cause them to return upon him for many years, with an abundance of [...]\n</li>\n<li>\nand may He reunite us with him in the best of circumstances, by His grace and subtle kindness, God willing.\n</li>\n<li>\nWhat he wishes to know is that I have investigated what you instructed me concerning, namely the news of Maghreb.\n</li>\n<li>\nAs for al-Mahdiyya, it remains in a state of safety. It was reported that two ships had departed from it:\n</li>\n<li>\none of them a ship belonging to the ruler of al-Mahdiyya, and the other a Byzantine ship. They also reported\n</li>\n<li>\nthat its prices are those of al-saqa\u1e6d [?], namely good and profitable prices,\n</li>\n<li>\nunlike al-Mariyya. As for Tripoli, after [...] there came concerning it the report\n</li>\n<li>\nwhich was concealed from no one. A trustworthy Muslim man was captured/taken, and he reported news that\n</li>\n<li>\nmatters had been resolved and that it had returned to Muslim control. We hope that this is indeed true by God\u2019s will.\n</li>\n<li>\nYour servant had sent [something] in the care of Ab\u016b l-\u1e24asan, and I ask your favor that\n</li>\n<li>\nyou send me some goods, among them a small quantity of brazilwood, at whatever price, provided that it is of good quality. If\n</li>\n<li>\nit is convenient to send something in his care, [do so]; otherwise send me one dinar\u2019s worth quickly, for I am without it.\n</li>\n<li>\nYour illustrious presence is especially greeted with the fullest peace. To Shaykh Ab\u016b \u02bfAl\u012b, the choicest greetings, and to his children,\n</li>\n<li>\ngreetings; and to my lord, the shaykh and ra\u02be\u012bs, the choicest greetings, and greetings to all those encompassed by his care.\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
